From 0e4103ffae3c44b425e0fca01eb9172f6125b860 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: andrei <root@i5.local>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:36:34 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] feat: extend MoE expert cache to fused
 gate_up/GELU/scaled experts with gated admission

- cache fused gate_up_exps layers (gemma4) and GELU experts; apply per-expert
  scales to the device chain by reusing the scale rows of the host chain
- gated admission: upload an expert after N misses within a W-token window,
  free slots fill on first miss (--moe-expert-cache-window/-admit)
- never schedule a second upload for an expert that is already in flight
- allocate the cache on the layer device instead of the router buffer type
- synchronize before publishing table updates; pin the host mul_mat_id ops
  to the CPU backend so op offload cannot double count cached experts
- observe routing through an op_params flag instead of a weight-name match
- report hit rate, uploads, upload bytes per step and evictions
